      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Temporomandibular joint dysfunctions may involve ophthalmic symptoms such as orbital pain, asthenopia, or anisocoria. These ophthalmic manifestations may be the first signs or the complications of masticatory system dysfunctions. Treatment of these ophthalmic symptoms begins with treatment of the temporomandibular joint dysfunctions."},
